# sock8 monorepo
This is the sock8 monorepo.

# Project overview
sock8 (sock8.com) is a WebSockets-as-a-Service SaaS built on Cloudflare Workers with Durable Objects and WebSocket Hibernation.
Our goal is to provide an outstanding developer experience for adding real-time features to an application.
We facilitate an amazing developer experience through tRPC-inspired end-to-end type-safety in our SDK. Our SDK provides easy-to-use functionality for interacting with our API to interact with WebSockets. We also provide drop-in Next.js functionality with our SDK so it is easy to add sock8 to a Next.js application with a few lines of code.

# Project structure
This is a Turborepo monorepo. It is separated into `apps/` and `packages/`.
Projects in the `apps/` directory are applications that are deployed.
Projects in the `packages/` directory are private re-usable workspace-scoped packages that provide shared functionality, utilities, etc.

- `apps/web` ([package.json](mdc:apps/web/package.json)) is our web application for sock8.com. It primarily uses React.js (Next.js) with TypeScript, shadcn/ui and TailwindCSS. shadcn/ui components are stored in the `@sock8/ui` package at `packages/ui`. Components from there should be re-used. This web application is deployed to Vercel. This website includes our landing page, marketing pages and dashboard.

- `apps/api` ([package.json](mdc:apps/worker/package.json)) is our Cloudflare Worker providing the end-user-facing API for sock8 (deployed to Cloudflare Workers at `api.sock8.com`). This provides our API but also our WebSocket connection management and infrastructure/functionality for our product (WebSockets-as-a-Service). We utilize Durable Objects and Websockets with Hibernation for our core product. We also make use of KV (Cloudflare Key-Value store) and R2 (Cloudflare AWS S3-compatible object/blob storage).

- `packages/auth` ([package.json](mdc:packages/auth/package.json)) is our shared authentication package used on our `web` and `api` applications for handling authentication-related operations. This is provided via Better-Auth.

- `packages/db` ([package.json](mdc:packages/db/package.json)) is our shared database schema. This is used in our `web` and `api` applications for shared database data, such as API Keys. The schema is defined using Drizzle. We use MySQL as our dialect and PlanetScale as our database provider. Because we use PlanetScale, we cannot use foreign key constraints.

- `packages/ui` ([package.json](mdc:packages/ui/package.json)) is our shared shadcn/ui components and other React.js components for use in our web application. Look here before creating new components.

Packages can be imported using `@sock8/<package-name>`. For example, to import the `Button` shadcn/ui component from `packages/ui`:
```typescript
import { Button } from "@sock8/ui/components/button";
```

# Tooling
- We use `bun` exclusively throughout the monorepo for all apps and packages as the package manager. Do NOT use npm, pnpm, or yarn.
- We use TypeScript throughout.
- We use MySQL via PlanetScale with Drizzle. See [schema.ts](mdc:packages/db/src/schema.ts)
- We use Better-Auth for authentication. See [auth.ts](mdc:packages/auth/src/auth.ts)
- We use shadcn/ui for base components in the web application. These are location in `packages/ui` and imported with `@sock8/ui/*`
- We use TailwindCSS in web applications for styling.

# Code Styles and Rules
- We use prettier code style. Respect our prettier and eslint rules.
- We use functional-style React.
- Always try and find an existing component or helper function for a use-case before creating a new one.
- We do not use foreign key constraints in our MySQL (drizzle/PlanetScale) database schemas.
- Never leave hanging or unused imports.
- Never leave unused variables. If an unused variable must be left, prefix the variable name with "_" so that it will be ignored by ESLint.
- Always fix all linter errors and warnings.

# Important Notes
- After adding or removing a package from a `package.json`, you MUST run `bun install` in the workspace.